    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** headlining the roster as our premier option. Boasting an elite efficiency score of 84.24, **Junior Caminero** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and a favorable matchup against Baz, placing him in a prime position to anchor our offensive production. Close behind, **Caleb Durbin** presents a high-upside play at 70.40, largely driven by an excellent matchup against the highly hittable Wilkinson (8.21 xERA). We are also banking on the speed-oriented ceiling of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.45); his projection remains aggressive due to his leadoff spot and a base-stealing opportunity presented by a pitcher with a famously slow delivery, effectively mitigating the risks posed by Miller, B.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Carson Benge**, who finished just shy of the starting cutoff with a 41.92 score. While his potential is evident, he was squeezed out of the lineup in favor of the higher-ceiling profiles of **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** and **Kyle Schwarber**, both of whom benefit from superior park and pitching matchups today. We remain cautious regarding **Yordan Alvarez**; despite an elite xwOBA, his score of 56.07 reflects a suppressive L/L platoon disadvantage against Basso, marking him as a marginal start who is only active due to his high-end talent. \n\nStrategic risks for the day include the L/L matchup for **Hector Rodriguez**, which keeps his efficiency at a modest 50.58, and the ongoing volatility surrounding our bench depth, as **Lars Nootbaar** and **Colt Keith** remain sidelined. We are monitoring **Kazuma Okamoto** closely, as his respectable 63.58 score is contingent on overcoming the veteran savvy of Rod\u00f3n. As we push for gains in our scarcest categories, the combination of **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** will be the primary engines for our SB goals, assuming they can exploit their respective pitcher-delivery vulnerabilities.",
